  install (): String => "```bash\n# Go\ngo get github.com/orbitmines/physics/languages/physics.go\n```"
  readme (): String => "# github.com/orbitmines/physics/languages/physics.go - Go\n\n> Generated by `npx ray gen` from [implementation/physics.ray](../../implementation/physics.ray/) and [implementation/gen](../../implementation/gen/). Do not edit - change the `.ray` and regenerate.\n\nThe physics library in Go: the theories and their rules, the continuous model derived from them (the medium), and the settings a simulation of sources - stars, planets, any bodies a theory has - is planned by. Back to the [project README](../../README.md).\n\n## Installation\n\n{Go.install}\n\nGo 1.22 or later. The package is `physics`.\n\n## Using it\n\nGo has no dynamic members, so a Ray object is reached by name: `physics.Get(x, \"name\")`, `physics.Call(x, \"method\", []any{{...}})`, `physics.Set(x, \"name\", value)`, `physics.Make(physics.Class, physics.Kw(\"field\", value), ...)`. Every value is an `any`: numbers are `float64`, lists `*physics.List` (their elements in `.Items`).\n\n```go\nimport . \"github.com/orbitmines/physics/languages/physics.go\"\n\n// a theory, and its continuous model on the CPU: a box of cells, the vacuum settled, one body in it\nmedium := Call(G, \"medium\", []any{{31.0, 96.0, 3.0, 8.0, 1.0}})\nSet(medium, \"local_rays\", true)\nCall(medium, \"add\", []any{{Make(Hole, Kw(\"x\", 15.0), Kw(\"y\", 15.0), Kw(\"mx\", 0.3), Kw(\"ways\", 1.0))}})\nGet(medium, \"seed\")\nfor t := 0; t < 5; t++ {{\n  Get(medium, \"tick\")\n}}\n```\n\n## A simulation of sources: the plan\n\nA run is set by a `Plan`: how many sources, how big a box, and four kinds of setting - `Resolution` (how finely the medium reads), `Budget` (how much of the device it may take), `Batching` (how a run larger than the device is carried) and `Output` (what comes back). The plan says what the device must hold before anything runs.\n\n```go\nplan := Make(Plan, Kw(\"sources\", 1e9), Kw(\"side\", 241.0))\nSet(Get(plan, \"budget\"), \"compact\", true)   // twelve bytes a source\nfmt.Println(Str(Call(plan, \"report\", []any{{16.0 * (1 << 30), float64(1 << 31)}})))\n```\n\n## Theorems\n\n`physics.Theorems()` is every theorem, keyed by theory and then by question, as JSON.\n\n## On the GPU\n\nThe GPU runtime of the medium is being carried into `.ray`, so that every language runs the same thing on every backend. Until then it runs from the [TypeScript package](../physics.ts/README.md).\n"
  gomod (): String => "// GENERATED by `npx ray gen` from implementation/physics.ray - do not edit\nmodule github.com/orbitmines/physics/languages/physics.go\n\ngo 1.22\n"
